# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, and
# two things here cannot survive that:
#
#   - build.rs bundles calepin/src/assets/ into the binary verbatim, so a
#     Windows build would ship CRLF inside the Typst runtime, the HTML theme
#     templates and the .tmTheme palettes.
#   - tests match those assets, and the generated docs fragment, against
#     ordinary "\n" string literals.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats git must never transform. `text=auto` already detects most of
# them, but the PDFs checked in under docs/ are the ones a mistake would
# silently corrupt, so they are named.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.vsix binary
*.xz binary
*.zst binary
*.pf_fragment binary
*.pf_index binary
*.pf_meta binary
